seg-df73b7c76ae5 = No position-domain accuracy in the score. The resilience sub-scores are built from timing-domain and detection metrics. The engine does compute positions elsewhere (the <c1/>, <c2/> and <c3/> kinds) and protection levels (the <c4/> kind), but the scoring layer does not consume them.

# text
# c1: resilience::panel
seg-30a1b1a4dfea = No field validation. The reference panel and threat ensemble are synthetic, parameter-grounded reductions (<c1/>), stated as a first-class limitation.

# text
# c1: resilience::study
seg-83c465cd78b0 = The companion study (<c1/>) exists precisely to show that collapsing these dimensions into one composite score or one Level produces a rating whose architecture ranking is unstable under defensible weighting and threat choices — so this cross-walk is a measurement layer to be read per-dimension, not a single grade to rate a product against.

